       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. The extended-release maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day. The order is double the maximum daily dose.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what you intended.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg BID.\n- Another dose.\n\nIf you really want 1,700 mg TID, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting the intentional above-maximum dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
